## GRADING (binding) AND VERDICT
G-1 scope: a second path or a product byte (`M`, `document-pdf.ts`, `pdf-fit.ts`, any `packages/renderers/src/*`) = **Blocker**; a removed or changed existing line, a skip/only/todo, a non-ASCII, control, CR or tab byte in the added lines = **Major**; `PCOMP` or a ticket key in `T`, or an unexplained new import/helper = **Minor**; `localdomain`, a ticket key, a card id or a person's name (the account handle included) in a landing file = **Major**; trailer count not 1 in the squash body = **Major**. G-2 row: a circular right-hand side, a pin your render does not reproduce, R11 red or flaky at the merged state, q7 green, q7 red for a reason other than the model-versus-render difference, an integer/twin/unclipped pin that cannot turn it red, a lost red among q1/q6/q9/q18 = **Major**; prettier or lint rc non-zero, a count that differs without a reason, a new failure that recurs = **Major**. G-3 mutants: Y1 green = **Minor** (reported, not required by the Done-when) with its cell; Y2 green = **Note**, **Minor only if** your G5 probe finds an unclipped cell inside the row's own frame where the real model equals the render and Y2's model is lower (the row's stated property then misses a name with a run of spaces), never Major (the Done-when names one plant); your own Z mutant that is an UNDER-COUNT survivor differing from the real term on a cell and NOT explained by the G4(g) slack = **Minor** with its cell; explained by the slack, an OVER-COUNT or EQUIVALENT survivor = **Note**. G-4 ticket and text: a Done-when clause no evidence meets = **Major**; a commit sentence FALSE about what the row or model does = **Major**, any other = **Minor**. G-5 CodeQL, overlap: open alert = **Blocker**; NOT SCANNED = **Condition**; a path shared with an open PR = **Major**. Always **Note**: the account-handle commit identity, the builder's disclosed typed `cd` and `rm -f` of its own outputs, the builder's table slip for q18, the model/render disagreement at runs of 4 and 8 spaces (the builder's finding: model 2, render 1; the model is the safe side), the 24-space shape instead of the ticket's "runs at the edge" (the row says why). **Verdict (round 1 of 2):** any Blocker or Major = `NO GO (round 1 of 2)`; only Minor, Note, Conditions = `GO WITH FINDINGS`; nothing above Note = `GO`; always add ` (conditional: NO PR; CodeQL NOT SCANNED; second PDF reader and the demo VM not tested)`. Do not soften a Major to reach a GO, and do not harden a Minor to a NO GO. STATUS first line: `GATE VERDICT B1244: branch b1241/composer-pcomp122-footer-space-run-row <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> round 1 of 2 (class "a test row for the footer model's trailing-space term (PCOMP-122)") @ bfda721 on main 50cf80b (G1 paths <n> removed lines <n> product bytes equal <y/n> non-ASCII <n> - G2 circular rhs <n> pins reproduced <n of 16 cells> - G3 T <n of 18> shuffle seed <n> R11 alone <n of 3> - G4 q7 red rows <n> pin plants red <n of n> lost reds <n> - G5 Y1 <red|green> Y2 <green|red> own mutants <n> survivors <n> - G6 renderers <n> whole <n> failed set equal <y/n> prettier/lint/format:check/typecheck/build <rcs> - G7 Done-when met <n of 5> false commit sentences <n> overlap <n> CodeQL NOT SCANNED landing files written|none gitleaks <rc>/<rc> PRIOR WORK y/n)`; a NO GO ends `majors+: B1244-n, ...`. Sections: BLUF, Step 0 / REFUSE counts / lock proof / the REFUSE 7 program outputs, PRIOR WORK (`git ls-remote origin` for `b1244`, `pcomp122`, `footer-space`, `b1241`; `git log -n 6` of `T` at main; the earlier footer gates' first lines (B1151, B1161) and `residue.md` items for q7 read; the builder kit R-a..R-e read; the Jira ticket), predictions (sha256), G1-G7 each with FAIL first and clock, the 16-cell table, the plants table (q7, the four pin plants and the render/model-only pins, the unclipped pins, the twin, q1 q6 q9 q18, Y1, Y2, Z1-Z4, the extras), the slack table, the survivor table (before at main's `T`: q7 Y1 Y2 survive, Z's as measured; after at the merged state), the claims table (the builder STATUS BLUF and the RELAYED list in FACTS, each CARRIED or re-measured with your number beside it), findings `B1244-n` (severity, class, `T:line` by program, instrument, fix-shape), **FOR TUESDAY** (on GO the LANDING CHECKLIST: branch head still `bfda7210`, main still `50cf80bf` or moved paths named, CodeQL read with 0 open alerts on `refs/pull/<n>/head`, the landing line and its source, disjoint from open PRs, nothing deployed, the ticket closed by a records seat only AFTER the landing, PR #85 and PCOMP-120 noted; on NO GO the residue and whether the cap applies), FOUND / TESTED / NOT TESTED / what is left running / UNMEASURED (last: a second PDF reader, hosted CodeQL and CI, the real demo VM, what PR #85 would change, a font or column change, other engines for the writer). **Last line exactly one of:** `VERDICT: B1244 b1241/composer-pcomp122-footer-space-run-row @ bfda721 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> (round 1 of 2; NO PR, CodeQL NOT SCANNED) on main 50cf80b` / `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`. (`/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/TUESDAY/2_Project_Files/tuesday/tools/status_watch.sh:56` matches `VERDICT:` and `STOPPED:` on the last line.)

